# Risk-accepted findings in the legacy GitBook 3.2.3 engine tree.
# Everything patchable is patched at image build by
# scripts/patch-vulnerable-deps.sh — the entries below have no fix that the
# engine survives (see the script's comments and issue #20).

# immutable 3.8.3 — engine's core data layer. immutable 4.x breaks the
# engine's Record definitions (verified: pages fail to render). Exposure is
# prototype-pollution via untrusted collection input; the engine only feeds
# it book content from the local filesystem.
CVE-2026-59879
CVE-2026-59880

# braces 1.8.5 / 2.3.2 — ReDoS through crafted glob patterns. Glob input
# comes from the book author's own config, not untrusted users. No fixed
# 1.x/2.x exists; braces 3 is incompatible with the chokidar 1.x consumers.
CVE-2024-4068

# ip 1.1.5 (nested in the engine's npm, used only by its SOCKS-proxy path,
# which this image never exercises) — upstream never shipped a fixed
# release for this CVE in any version.
CVE-2024-29415
